<title>GERMANY: GEC Alsthom unit wins Czech turbine bid.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom unit wins Czech turbine bid.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French railway engineering group GEC-Alsthom said its subsidiary European Gas Turbines GmbH had won a 30 million mark contract to deliver a 70 megawatt gas turbine to the Czech Republic.</p>
<p>The client and general contractor for the power plant project is Noell-KRC Energie- und Umwelttechnik GmbH of Schkeuditz.</p>
<p>The combined-cycle power plant will supply the city of Usti with district heat as well as electric power. The gas turbine is to be delivered in early 1998, and the power plant will begin operations.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
